WHAT IS MEASURED AND WHAT IS NOT

Measured, on a simulator running in one process on a laptop CPU: the bytes each
of 32 simulated devices holds per category (from the real size of every tensor
allocated), the bytes every ring collective sends per device and per link, the
forward and backward FLOPs torch's counter records, the number of weights each
device's optimiser updates, and the trained weights. Scale: a 666,560-weight
model, four training steps.

Not measured: any time. The times in RESULTS.md come from ASSUMED link
bandwidths and an ASSUMED device throughput set in config.py. The memory ladder
for a 30-billion-weight model is arithmetic from the formulas, not a run, and
its 80 GB card capacity is an assumed figure. Activations are excluded from
every memory number.

ZeRO itself is the published design of its authors; this exercise reimplements
its storage arrangement to measure it and claims no part of the design.
